You have a JSON file containing pairs of queries and links. Please create a
table displaying the query, the corresponding link, and your semantic similarity
assessment between the query and a website pointed by the link, as a real number
between 0 and 1.0. A score of 0 means they are completely unrelated, while 1.0
indicates they are identical in meaning. Do the assessments for all the pairs
from the document. Do not scale results for only the pairs in the document.
Focus solely on the semantic comparison, not syntax or keyword matching. Just
use your mind, do not try to use some code or library. I expect your comparison
will be very deterministic.

At the end, show the average and median similarity scores for all pairs in the
file. Additionally, highlight the 5 most similar and 5 least similar pairs
(full query text and corresponding full website link). Do not complain, I know
You can do this. Don't be lazy, do all the job and do not miss any pair from
the document. Create a markdown file with the whole result.
